      "warning": "Approximate marketing-plan-derived townhome envelopes, not surveyed architectural models. Seven June footprints and three additional highlighted blocks in the currently linked image are registered through two City street junctions and four common roof centroids. The image scale bar conflicts with City junction spacing by about 25%; City coordinates control the model scale. Estimated placement \u00b110 m and roof-outline tolerance \u00b13 m are interpretive, not statistical confidence bounds. All ten envelopes use an estimated 13 m maximum with \u00b13.5 m uncertainty, derived from about 6.2 m registered bay width and roughly 2.1:1 height-to-bay proportions in the official illustrative facade. No published dimensional height was found. Roofs, balconies, basements and facade articulation are omitted; grey marketing roofs are retained from the June version, not independently confirmed current building drawings.",
